1
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:12,596
So what is it?
What's wrong?

2
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:15,766
I don't know. Some kind
of signal, drawing the Tardis off course.

3
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:17,143
Where are we?

4
00:00:17,226 --> 00:00:19,270
Earth. Utah, North America.

5
00:00:19,687 --> 00:00:21,022
About half a mile underground.

6
00:00:21,105 --> 00:00:23,274
And when are we?

7
00:00:24,275 --> 00:00:25,443
2012.

8
00:00:26,652 --> 00:00:29,113
God, that's so close. I should be 26!

9
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:35,953
Blimey.

10
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:39,123
Like a great big museum.

11
00:00:40,416 --> 00:00:42,084
An alien museum.

12
00:00:43,544 --> 00:00:45,171
Someone's got a hobby.

13
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:48,382
They must've spent a fortune on this.

14
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:51,594
Chunks of meteorite. Moondust.

15
00:00:51,927 --> 00:00:53,971
That's the milometer
from the Roswell spaceship.

16
00:00:55,306 --> 00:00:56,599
That's a bit of Slitheen!

17
00:00:56,682 --> 00:00:58,726
That's a Slitheen's arm,
it's been stuffed!

18
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:02,646
Ah, look at you!

19
00:01:13,491 --> 00:01:14,658
What is it?

20
00:01:15,076 --> 00:01:18,079
An old friend of mine. Well, enemy.

21
00:01:19,038 --> 00:01:21,290
The stuff of nightmares,
reduced to an exhibit.

22
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,001
I'm getting old.

23
00:01:24,668 --> 00:01:26,337
Is that where the signal's coming from?

24
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:29,298
Nah, it's stone-dead. The signal's alive.

25
00:01:30,299 --> 00:01:31,717
Something's reaching out.

26
00:01:32,176 --> 00:01:33,511
Calling for help.

27
00:01:49,485 --> 00:01:52,530
If someone's
collecting aliens, that makes you Exhibit A.

28
00:02:34,107 --> 00:02:35,525
<i>Attention all personnel.</i>

29
00:02:35,608 --> 00:02:38,945
<i>Bad Wolf 1 descending,
Bad Wolf 1 descending.</i>

30
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:49,253
On behalf of all of us,
I wanna wish you a very happy birthday, sir.

31
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,797
And the President
called to convey his personal best wishes.

32
00:02:51,881 --> 00:02:54,175
The President is
10 points down, I want him replaced.

33
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:56,760
I don't think that's very wise, sir.

34
00:02:56,844 --> 00:02:58,429
Thank you so much
for your opinion, you're fired.

35
00:02:58,512 --> 00:02:59,805
- Get rid of him.
- What?

36
00:02:59,889 --> 00:03:01,849
Wipe his memory.
Put him on the road someplace.

37
00:03:01,974 --> 00:03:04,602
Memphis, Minneapolis.
Somewhere beginning with "M."

38
00:03:04,727 --> 00:03:07,271
So, the next President, what do you think?
Republican or Democrat?

39
00:03:07,396 --> 00:03:08,939
- Democrat, sir.
- For what reason?

40
00:03:09,732 --> 00:03:11,775
They're just so funny, sir?

41
00:03:13,569 --> 00:03:15,404
- What is your name?
- Goddard, sir.

42
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:16,947
Diana Goddard.

43
00:03:18,449 --> 00:03:19,825
I like you, Diana Goddard.

44
00:03:20,326 --> 00:03:22,620
- So where's the English kid?
- Sir, sir!

45
00:03:23,245 --> 00:03:25,039
I bought 10 more artifacts
at auction, Mr. Van Statten.

46
00:03:25,122 --> 00:03:26,248
Bring 'em on. Let me see 'em.

47
00:03:26,332 --> 00:03:28,417
Uh, sir, with respect,
there's something more urgent.

48
00:03:28,626 --> 00:03:32,296
We arrested two intruders, 53 floors down.
We don't know how they got in.

49
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:34,256
I'll tell you how they got in. In-tru-da window!

50
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,508
In-tru-da window, that was funny!

51
00:03:37,968 --> 00:03:39,220
Bring 'em in. Let's see 'em.

52
00:03:39,303 --> 00:03:41,722
And tell Simmons I want to visit my little pet.
Get to it.

53
00:03:42,473 --> 00:03:45,559
Simmons, you'd better give me good news!
Is it talking?

54
00:03:53,234 --> 00:03:56,070
- Not exactly talking, no.
- Then what's it doing?

55
00:03:56,153 --> 00:03:57,154
Screaming.

56
00:03:57,238 --> 00:03:58,572
Is that any good?

57
00:04:01,158 --> 00:04:02,451
And this is the last.

58
00:04:03,077 --> 00:04:04,578
Paid $800,000 for it.

59
00:04:04,912 --> 00:04:05,913
What does it do?

60
00:04:06,664 --> 00:04:08,582
Well, you see the tubes on the side?

61
00:04:08,666 --> 00:04:11,085
Must be to channel something,
I think maybe fuel.

62
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:12,544
I really wouldn't hold it like that.

63
00:04:12,628 --> 00:04:15,130
- Shut it!
- Really though, that's wrong.

64
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:16,924
Is it dangerous?

65
00:04:17,007 --> 00:04:18,384
No, it just looks silly.

66
00:04:29,353 --> 00:04:30,938
You just need to be...

67
00:04:33,691 --> 00:04:35,150
...delicate.

68
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,117
It's a musical instrument.

69
00:04:45,828 --> 00:04:47,037
And it's a long way from home.

70
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:48,539
Here, let me.

71
00:04:50,416 --> 00:04:51,667
I did say delicate.

72
00:04:52,543 --> 00:04:55,004
It reacts to the
smallest fingerprint.

73
00:04:56,005 --> 00:04:57,214
It needs precision.

74
00:05:02,344 --> 00:05:04,555
Very good. Quite the expert.

75
00:05:05,431 --> 00:05:06,473
As are you.

76
00:05:07,933 --> 00:05:09,476
Who exactly are you?

77
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:12,563
I'm the Doctor. And who are you?

78
00:05:12,688 --> 00:05:13,814
Like you don't know!

79
00:05:14,273 --> 00:05:16,650
We're hidden away with the
most valuable collection

80
00:05:16,734 --> 00:05:19,570
of extraterrestrial artifacts in the world,

81
00:05:19,695 --> 00:05:22,239
and you just stumbled in by mistake.

82
00:05:22,364 --> 00:05:24,325
Pretty much
sums me up, yeah.

83
00:05:24,742 --> 00:05:26,243
Question is, how did you get in?

84
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:30,789
53 floors down, with your
little cat-burglar accomplice.

85
00:05:30,998 --> 00:05:33,000
Quite a collector yourself, she's rather pretty.

86
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:35,586
She's gonna smack you
if you keep calling her "she."

87
00:05:35,919 --> 00:05:37,588
She's English, too!

88
00:05:37,796 --> 00:05:40,007
Hey, Little Lord Fauntleroy,
got you a girlfriend.

89
00:05:40,758 --> 00:05:42,468
This is Mr. Henry van Statten.

90
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:44,219
And who's he when he's at home?

91
00:05:44,303 --> 00:05:46,096
Mr. Van Statten owns the internet.

92
00:05:46,430 --> 00:05:48,849
Don't be stupid. No one owns the Internet.

93
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:51,602
Let's just keep the
whole world thinking that way, right, kids?

94
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:54,146
So you're just about an expert in everything,

95
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,272
except the things in your museum.

96
00:05:55,481 --> 00:05:57,191
Anything you don't understand, you lock up.

97
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:58,525
And you claim greater knowledge?

98
00:05:58,609 --> 00:06:00,444
I don't need to make claims.
I know how good I am.

99
00:06:00,569 --> 00:06:03,447
And yet I captured you right next to the Cage.

100
00:06:04,239 --> 00:06:05,366
What were you doing down there?

101
00:06:05,449 --> 00:06:06,450
You tell me.

102
00:06:06,575 --> 00:06:09,370
The Cage contains my one living specimen.

103
00:06:09,453 --> 00:06:10,954
- And what's that?
- Like you don't know.

104
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:12,456
- Show me.
- You wanna see it?

105
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,958
Blimey, you can smell the testosterone.

106
00:06:15,751 --> 00:06:18,379
Goddard! Inform the Cage
we're heading down.

107
00:06:18,587 --> 00:06:20,255
You, English, look after the girl.

108
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:23,717
Go and canoodle or spoon
or whatever it is you British do.

109
00:06:23,801 --> 00:06:26,095
And you, Doctor with no name.

110
00:06:27,721 --> 00:06:29,181
Come and see my pet!

111
00:06:32,434 --> 00:06:34,019
We've tried everything.

112
00:06:34,353 --> 00:06:39,942
The creature has shielded
itself, but there's definite signs of life inside.

113
00:06:40,359 --> 00:06:41,985
Inside? Inside what?

114
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:43,070
Welcome back, sir!

115
00:06:43,654 --> 00:06:46,490
I've had to take
the power down, the Metaltron is resting.

116
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:47,825
Metaltron?

117
00:06:48,158 --> 00:06:50,160
Thought of it myself. Good, isn't it?

118
00:06:50,661 --> 00:06:53,122
Although I'd much prefer
to find out its real name.

119
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:55,124
Here, you'd better put these on.

120
00:06:55,249 --> 00:06:56,667
The last guy that touched it

121
00:06:58,043 --> 00:06:59,253
burst into flames.

122
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:01,380
I won't touch it, then.

123
00:07:03,132 --> 00:07:04,466
Go ahead, Doctor.

124
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:05,843
Impress me.

125
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:20,107
Don't open that door until we get a result.

126
00:07:34,913 --> 00:07:36,165
Look, I'm sorry about this.

127
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:39,251
Mr. Van Statten
might think he's clever, but never mind him.

128
00:07:39,626 --> 00:07:41,795
I've come to help. I'm the Doctor.

129
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:45,340
Doctor.

130
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:48,427
Impossible!

131
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:51,430
The Doctor?

132
00:07:54,892 --> 00:07:56,560
Exterminate!

133
00:07:56,894 --> 00:07:58,395
Exterminate!

134
00:07:58,604 --> 00:07:59,646
Let me out!

135
00:07:59,855 --> 00:08:00,898
Exterminate!

136
00:08:01,732 --> 00:08:03,901
- Sir, it's going to kill him!
- It's talking!

137
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:06,737
You are an enemy of the Daleks.

138
00:08:07,488 --> 00:08:09,323
You must be destroyed!

139
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:17,247
It's not working.

140
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,256
Fantastic!

141
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,634
Oh, fantastic!

142
00:08:30,052 --> 00:08:31,929
Powerless.
Look at you.

143
00:08:32,763 --> 00:08:35,807
The great space dustbin. How does it feel?

144
00:08:35,891 --> 00:08:37,392
Keep back!

145
00:08:37,476 --> 00:08:38,602
What for?

146
00:08:38,727 --> 00:08:40,270
What are you gonna do to me?

147
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:46,568
If you can't kill,

148
00:08:48,529 --> 00:08:50,447
then what are you good for, Dalek?

149
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:53,283
What's the point of you?

150
00:08:55,953 --> 00:08:57,621
You're nothing.

151
00:08:58,455 --> 00:08:59,998
<i>What the hell
are you here for?</i>

152
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:03,919
I am waiting for orders.</i>

153
00:09:04,002 --> 00:09:07,256
- What does that mean?
- I am a soldier.

154
00:09:07,339 --> 00:09:10,717
I was bred to receive orders.

155
00:09:10,801 --> 00:09:13,220
Well, you're never gonna get any. Not ever.

156
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:15,597
I demand orders!

157
00:09:15,681 --> 00:09:18,225
They're never gonna come. Your race is dead.

158
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:21,436
You all burnt. All of you.
Ten million ships on fire.

159
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:25,148
The entire Dalek race
wiped out, in one second.

160
00:09:25,315 --> 00:09:26,483
You lie!

161
00:09:26,608 --> 00:09:27,693
I watched it happen.

162
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:28,986
<i>I made it happen.</i>

163
00:09:29,152 --> 00:09:31,446
You destroyed us?

164
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:43,500
I had no choice.

165
00:09:43,834 --> 00:09:48,130
And what of the Time Lords?

166
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:54,761
Dead.

167
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:57,097
They burnt with you.

168
00:09:57,222 --> 00:09:59,766
The end of the Last Great Time War.

169
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:02,853
Everyone lost.

170
00:10:04,271 --> 00:10:08,442
And the coward survived.

171
00:10:08,525 --> 00:10:11,778
Oh, and I caught your little signal.

172
00:10:12,613 --> 00:10:15,616
"Help me." Poor little thing.

173
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:21,371
But there's no one else
coming 'cause there's no one else left.

174
00:10:21,913 --> 00:10:27,878
I am alone in the universe.

175
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:30,380
Yep.

176
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,676
So are you.

177
00:10:36,637 --> 00:10:39,514
We are the same.

178
00:10:40,057 --> 00:10:42,392
We're not the same! I'm not...

179
00:10:44,061 --> 00:10:45,562
No, wait.

180
00:10:46,688 --> 00:10:48,231
Maybe we are.

181
00:10:49,191 --> 00:10:50,525
You're right! Yeah, okay!

182
00:10:51,193 --> 00:10:52,527
You've got a point.

183
00:10:52,986 --> 00:10:54,279
'Cause I know what to do.

184
00:10:55,072 --> 00:10:56,657
I know what should happen.

185
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,867
I know what you deserve.

186
00:11:02,079 --> 00:11:03,455
Exterminate.

187
00:11:07,125 --> 00:11:08,960
Have pity!

188
00:11:09,044 --> 00:11:11,254
Why should I? You never did!

189
00:11:12,464 --> 00:11:13,590
Get him out!

190
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:15,842
Help me!

191
00:11:17,511 --> 00:11:19,054
I saved your life.

192
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:21,890
Now talk to me. God damn it, talk to me!

193
00:11:21,973 --> 00:11:23,600
You've got to destroy it!

194
00:11:24,226 --> 00:11:26,311
The last in the universe.

195
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,939
<i>And now I know your name.</i>

196
00:11:29,606 --> 00:11:30,982
<i>Dalek.</i>

197
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:33,276
<i>Speak to me, Dalek!</i>

198
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:38,156
I am Henry van Statten, now recognize me!

199
00:11:42,953 --> 00:11:45,288
Make it talk again, Simmons.

200
00:11:45,956 --> 00:11:47,708
Whatever it takes.

201
00:11:51,628 --> 00:11:53,171
Sorry about the mess.

202
00:11:53,255 --> 00:11:55,841
Mr. Van Statten sort of lets me
do my own thing,

203
00:11:56,425 --> 00:11:58,552
so long as I deliver the goods.

204
00:11:59,136 --> 00:12:01,930
What do you think that is?

205
00:12:06,017 --> 00:12:07,018
Uhh.

206
00:12:07,144 --> 00:12:09,312
- A lump of metal?
- Yeah.

207
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:10,772
Yeah, but I think...

208
00:12:10,897 --> 00:12:14,609
Well, I'm almost certain,
it's from the hull of a spacecraft.

209
00:12:15,485 --> 00:12:20,073
The thing is, it's all true, everything the
United Nations tries to keep quiet.

210
00:12:21,032 --> 00:12:23,994
Spacecraft, aliens, visitors to Earth.

211
00:12:24,995 --> 00:12:26,121
They really exist.

212
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:27,497
That's amazing.

213
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:28,874
I know it sounds incredible.

214
00:12:28,999 --> 00:12:32,627
But I honestly believe
the whole universe is just teeming with life.

215
00:12:33,003 --> 00:12:34,921
I'm gobsmacked, yeah.

216
00:12:36,131 --> 00:12:38,467
And you do what? Sit here and catalog it?

217
00:12:39,301 --> 00:12:40,677
Best job in the world!

218
00:12:41,011 --> 00:12:43,180
Imagine if you could get out there.

219
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:45,891
Travel amongst the stars and see it for real.

220
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:48,268
Yeah. I'd give anything.

221
00:12:48,852 --> 00:12:51,104
I don't think it's ever gonna happen.
Not in our lifetimes.

222
00:12:51,188 --> 00:12:52,314
Oh, you never know.

223
00:12:52,606 --> 00:12:55,817
What about all those people who say they've
been inside of spaceships and things,

224
00:12:55,901 --> 00:12:57,527
and talked to aliens?

225
00:12:59,321 --> 00:13:00,530
I think they're nutters.

226
00:13:01,198 --> 00:13:02,365
Yeah. Me, too.

227
00:13:05,494 --> 00:13:06,787
So how d'you end up here?

228
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,997
Van Statten has agents all over the world,

229
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,123
looking for geniuses to recruit.

230
00:13:10,207 --> 00:13:12,125
Oh, right, you're a genius.

231
00:13:12,501 --> 00:13:13,919
Sorry, but, yeah.

232
00:13:14,002 --> 00:13:15,921
I can't help it, I was born clever.

233
00:13:17,214 --> 00:13:20,091
When I was eight,
I logged onto the US defense system.

234
00:13:20,467 --> 00:13:22,052
Nearly caused World War Three.

235
00:13:22,135 --> 00:13:23,428
What, and that's funny, is it?

236
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:26,306
You should've been there.
Just to see them running about.

237
00:13:26,389 --> 00:13:27,516
Fantastic!

238
00:13:29,226 --> 00:13:30,811
You sound like the Doctor.

239
00:13:31,228 --> 00:13:33,313
- Are you and him...
- No, we're just friends.

240
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:34,523
Good.

241
00:13:35,106 --> 00:13:36,399
Why's that good?

242
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,276
Just is.

243
00:13:41,071 --> 00:13:45,325
So, wouldn't you rather be downstairs?

244
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:47,994
You've got these bits of metal and stuff,

245
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:50,497
but Mr. Van Statten's got
a living creature down there.

246
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,834
Yeah. Well, I did ask,
but he keeps it to himself.

247
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:57,170
Although, if you're a genius,

248
00:13:57,254 --> 00:13:59,714
it doesn't take long to patch
through on the comms system.

249
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:02,092
Let's have a look then!

250
00:14:04,928 --> 00:14:07,556
It doesn't do much, the alien.

251
00:14:08,181 --> 00:14:10,934
It's weird, it's kind of useless.

252
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:14,271
It's just like this great big pepper pot.

253
00:14:25,615 --> 00:14:27,117
It's being tortured. Where's the Doctor?

254
00:14:28,118 --> 00:14:30,120
- I don't know.
- Take me down there. Now.

255
00:14:32,289 --> 00:14:33,415
The metal's just battle armor.

256
00:14:33,498 --> 00:14:35,041
The real Dalek creature is inside.

257
00:14:35,125 --> 00:14:36,626
- What does it look like?
- A nightmare.

258
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:39,671
It's a mutation.
The Dalek race were genetically engineered.

259
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:42,173
Every single emotion
was removed, except hate.

260
00:14:42,257 --> 00:14:45,427
Genetically engineered? By whom?

261
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:46,803
By a genius, Van Statten.

262
00:14:47,053 --> 00:14:49,639
By a man who was
king of his own little world. You'd like him.

263
00:14:49,723 --> 00:14:51,725
It's been on Earth for over 50 years.

264
00:14:51,808 --> 00:14:55,103
Sold at private auction,
moving from one collection to another.

265
00:14:55,186 --> 00:14:56,438
Why would it be a threat now?

266
00:14:56,521 --> 00:14:59,274
Because I'm here. How did it get to Earth?
Does anyone know?

267
00:14:59,357 --> 00:15:01,902
The records say it came
from the sky like a meteorite.

268
00:15:01,985 --> 00:15:04,070
It fell to Earth on the Ascension Islands,

269
00:15:04,154 --> 00:15:05,655
burnt in its crater for three days,

270
00:15:05,739 --> 00:15:06,907
before anybody could get near it.

271
00:15:06,990 --> 00:15:10,327
And all that time, it was screaming.
Must have gone insane.

272
00:15:12,954 --> 00:15:15,415
It must have fallen through time.
The only survivor.

273
00:15:15,498 --> 00:15:16,625
You talked about a war?

274
00:15:16,708 --> 00:15:20,420
The Time War. The final battle
between my people and the Dalek race.

275
00:15:20,629 --> 00:15:22,047
But you survived, too.

276
00:15:22,672 --> 00:15:23,798
Not by choice.

277
00:15:23,882 --> 00:15:27,969
This means the Dalek
isn't the only alien on Earth, Doctor.

278
00:15:28,053 --> 00:15:29,054
There's you.

279
00:15:29,137 --> 00:15:32,349
The only one of your kind in existence.

280
00:15:42,692 --> 00:15:44,277
Now smile!

281
00:15:49,032 --> 00:15:51,076
TWO hearts.

282
00:15:51,159 --> 00:15:52,702
A binary vascular system!

283
00:15:52,869 --> 00:15:54,537
Oh, I am so gonna patent this.

284
00:15:54,871 --> 00:15:56,373
So that's your secret.

285
00:15:56,498 --> 00:15:58,792
You don't just collect
this stuff, you scavenge it.

286
00:15:58,875 --> 00:16:02,754
This technology
has been falling to Earth for centuries.

287
00:16:02,837 --> 00:16:06,174
All it took was the right mind
to use it properly.

288
00:16:07,634 --> 00:16:10,387
Oh, the advances I've made from alien junk.

289
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:12,180
You have no idea, Doctor!

290
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:14,057
Broadband? Roswell.

291
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:18,979
Just last year, my scientists
cultivated bacteria

292
00:16:19,062 --> 00:16:21,773
from the Russian crater,
and do you know what we found?

293
00:16:22,399 --> 00:16:25,026
The cure for the common cold.

294
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:30,907
Kept it strictly within the laboratory, of
course. No need to get people excited.

295
00:16:31,032 --> 00:16:34,869
Why sell one cure
when I can sell a thousand palliatives?

296
00:16:34,953 --> 00:16:37,080
D'you know what a Dalek is, Van Statten?

297
00:16:39,165 --> 00:16:40,500
A Dalek is honest.

298
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:43,920
It does what it was
born to do, for the survival of its species.

299
00:16:44,004 --> 00:16:46,339
That creature in your dungeon
is better than you.

300
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:49,050
In that case,
I will be true to myself.

301
00:16:49,592 --> 00:16:50,927
And continue.

302
00:16:51,553 --> 00:16:55,598
Listen to me! That thing
downstairs is gonna kill every last one of us!

303
00:16:55,682 --> 00:16:57,350
Nothing can escape the Cage.

304
00:17:01,021 --> 00:17:04,315
But it's woken up!
It knows I'm here! It's gonna get out!

305
00:17:04,441 --> 00:17:07,986
Van Statten, I swear,
no one on this base is safe.

306
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:09,446
No one on this planet!

307
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:15,035
Hold it right there. Level three access.

308
00:17:15,118 --> 00:17:17,203
Special clearance from Mr. Van Statten.

309
00:17:21,374 --> 00:17:23,209
Don't get too close.

310
00:17:36,389 --> 00:17:37,432
Hello?

311
00:17:39,726 --> 00:17:41,227
Are you in pain?

312
00:17:41,352 --> 00:17:42,729
My name's Rose Tyler.

313
00:17:42,812 --> 00:17:44,898
I've got a friend, he can help.
He's called the Doctor.

314
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:46,316
What's your name?

315
00:17:46,816 --> 00:17:48,026
Yes.

316
00:17:49,319 --> 00:17:50,320
What?

317
00:17:52,989 --> 00:17:55,992
I am in pain.

318
00:17:57,243 --> 00:17:59,662
They torture me,

319
00:18:00,997 --> 00:18:05,335
but still they fear me.

320
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:08,296
Do you fear me?

321
00:18:10,215 --> 00:18:11,341
No.

322
00:18:15,428 --> 00:18:19,140
I am dying.

323
00:18:19,307 --> 00:18:20,934
No, we can help.

324
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:24,938
I welcome death.

325
00:18:26,147 --> 00:18:28,942
But I am glad

326
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:33,905
that before I die,

327
00:18:35,198 --> 00:18:38,159
I met a human

328
00:18:38,243 --> 00:18:41,621
who was not afraid.

329
00:18:42,539 --> 00:18:44,666
Isn't there anything I can do?

330
00:18:46,209 --> 00:18:48,711
My race is dead.

331
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:53,883
I shall die alone.

332
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:04,352
Rose, no!

333
00:19:06,312 --> 00:19:11,192
Genetic material extrapolated.

334
00:19:11,276 --> 00:19:15,989
Initiate cellular reconstruction!

335
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:24,581
What the hell have you done?

336
00:19:28,585 --> 00:19:31,504
What ya gonna do? Sucker me to death?

337
00:19:35,717 --> 00:19:36,968
It's killing him! Do something!

338
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:38,136
Condition red. Condition red.

339
00:19:38,261 --> 00:19:39,637
<i>I repeat, this is not a drill!</i>

340
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:43,433
Release me if you want to live.

341
00:19:46,186 --> 00:19:47,604
You've got to keep it in that cell!

342
00:19:47,979 --> 00:19:49,147
<i>Doctor, it's all my fault.</i>

343
00:19:49,272 --> 00:19:50,690
<i>I've sealed the compartment.</i>

344
00:19:50,773 --> 00:19:52,692
<i>It can't get out.
That lock's got a billion combinations.</i>

345
00:19:52,775 --> 00:19:53,776
The Dalek's a genius.

346
00:19:53,902 --> 00:19:57,614
It can calculate a thousand
billion combinations in one second flat.

347
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:20,261
Open fire!

348
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:23,723
Don't shoot it.
I want it unharmed!

349
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,350
Rose, get out of there!

350
00:20:33,650 --> 00:20:36,236
De Maggio, take the civilians
and get them out alive.

351
00:20:36,361 --> 00:20:37,654
That is your job, got that?

352
00:20:38,112 --> 00:20:39,280
You! With me!

353
00:20:58,967 --> 00:21:00,718
Abandoning the Cage, sir!

354
00:21:01,928 --> 00:21:04,847
We're losing power. It's draining the base.

355
00:21:04,931 --> 00:21:06,140
Oh, my God.

356
00:21:06,224 --> 00:21:08,768
It's draining the entire
power supplies of the whole of Utah.

357
00:21:08,851 --> 00:21:10,687
- It's downloading.
- Downloading what?

358
00:21:11,312 --> 00:21:13,523
Sir! The entire West Coast has gone down!

359
00:21:13,606 --> 00:21:17,527
It's not just energy.
That Dalek just absorbed the entire Internet.

360
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:19,112
It knows everything!

361
00:21:20,697 --> 00:21:25,076
The Daleks survive in me!

362
00:21:34,877 --> 00:21:36,337
The cameras in the vault have gone down.

363
00:21:36,421 --> 00:21:38,798
We've only got emergency power.
It's eaten everything else.

364
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:40,216
You've got to kill it now!

365
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:42,552
All guards to converge on the
Metaltron Cage immediately.

366
00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:46,264
Civilians! Let 'em through!

367
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,478
Cover the north wall.

368
00:21:52,562 --> 00:21:55,189
Red division, maintain
suppressing fire along the perimeter.

369
00:21:55,273 --> 00:21:57,358
Blue division...

370
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:30,224
Tell them to stop shooting at it.

371
00:22:30,308 --> 00:22:31,434
But it's killing them!

372
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:34,354
They're dispensable, that Dalek is unique.

373
00:22:34,437 --> 00:22:37,982
I don't want a scratch on its bodywork!
Do you hear me?

374
00:22:39,067 --> 00:22:40,651
Do you hear me?

375
00:22:57,126 --> 00:22:59,003
That's us,
right below the surface.

376
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:01,422
That's the Cage, and that's the Dalek.

377
00:23:01,506 --> 00:23:03,800
This museum of yours.
Have you got any alien weapons?

378
00:23:03,883 --> 00:23:06,469
Lots of them, but the trouble is
the Dalek's between us and them.

379
00:23:06,677 --> 00:23:08,054
We've got to keep that thing alive.

380
00:23:08,137 --> 00:23:10,098
We could just
seal the entire vault, trap it down there.

381
00:23:10,223 --> 00:23:11,432
Leaving everyone trapped with it?

382
00:23:11,516 --> 00:23:14,519
Rose is down there.
I won't let that happen, have you got that?

383
00:23:15,144 --> 00:23:16,813
It has to go through this area. What's that?

384
00:23:17,063 --> 00:23:18,147
Weapons testing.

385
00:23:18,231 --> 00:23:20,983
Give guns to technicians,
the lawyers, anyone, everyone.

386
00:23:21,067 --> 00:23:23,403
Only then have you got a chance of killing it.

387
00:23:25,613 --> 00:23:27,532
Stairs! That's more like it!

388
00:23:27,615 --> 00:23:28,825
Hasn't got legs, it's stuck!

389
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:30,410
It's coming! Get up!

390
00:23:46,342 --> 00:23:48,553
<i>Great big alien
death machine.</i>

391
00:23:48,636 --> 00:23:50,805
<i>Defeated by a flight of stairs!</i>

392
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:53,641
<i>Now listen to me.</i>

393
00:23:54,517 --> 00:23:56,602
I demand that you return to your Cage.

394
00:23:56,686 --> 00:23:57,937
If you want to negotiate,

395
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:00,523
then I can guarantee
Mr. Van Statten will be willing to talk.

396
00:24:00,606 --> 00:24:02,316
I accept that we imprisoned you,

397
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:04,026
and maybe that was wrong,

398
00:24:04,152 --> 00:24:07,613
but people have died,
and that stops right now.

399
00:24:08,739 --> 00:24:10,867
The killing stops. Have you got that?

400
00:24:11,367 --> 00:24:13,453
I demand that you surrender. Is that clear?

401
00:24:15,037 --> 00:24:17,248
Elevate.

402
00:24:24,505 --> 00:24:26,090
Oh, my God.

403
00:24:32,096 --> 00:24:33,514
Adam, get her out of here.

404
00:24:35,933 --> 00:24:37,226
Come with us. You can't stop it.

405
00:24:37,310 --> 00:24:39,937
Someone's got to try. Now get out!

406
00:24:40,021 --> 00:24:42,106
Don't look back, just run!

407
00:24:54,911 --> 00:24:56,954
I thought you were the great expert, Doctor.

408
00:24:57,330 --> 00:25:00,625
If you're so impressive,
then why not just reason with this Dalek?

409
00:25:01,250 --> 00:25:02,460
It must be willing to negotiate.

410
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:04,253
There must be something it needs.

411
00:25:04,337 --> 00:25:05,379
Everything needs something.

412
00:25:05,463 --> 00:25:07,173
- What's the nearest town?
- Salt Lake City.

413
00:25:07,256 --> 00:25:08,508
- Population?
- One million.

414
00:25:08,591 --> 00:25:09,675
All dead.

415
00:25:09,759 --> 00:25:12,053
If the Dalek gets out,
it'll murder every living creature.

416
00:25:12,136 --> 00:25:14,013
- That's all it needs.
- But why would it do that?

417
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:15,681
Because it honestly believes they should die.

418
00:25:15,765 --> 00:25:18,518
Human beings are different,
and anything different is wrong.

419
00:25:18,601 --> 00:25:20,394
It's the ultimate in racial cleansing,

420
00:25:20,478 --> 00:25:22,772
and you, Van Statten, you've let it loose.

421
00:25:33,282 --> 00:25:35,034
The Dalek's surrounded by a force field.

422
00:25:35,117 --> 00:25:36,953
The bullets are melting
before they even hit home.

423
00:25:37,078 --> 00:25:38,579
But it's not indestructible.

424
00:25:38,663 --> 00:25:41,374
<i>If you concentrate your
fire, you might get through.</i>

425
00:25:46,587 --> 00:25:48,339
<i>Aim for the dome, the head, the eyepiece.</i>

426
00:25:48,422 --> 00:25:49,632
That's the weak spot.

427
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:53,219
Thank you, Doctor, but I think I know
how to fight one single tin robot.

428
00:25:56,806 --> 00:25:57,807
Positions!

429
00:26:06,941 --> 00:26:08,526
Hold your fire!

430
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:11,654
You two, get the hell out of there!

431
00:26:37,597 --> 00:26:38,764
It was looking at me.

432
00:26:38,848 --> 00:26:40,224
Yeah, it wants to slaughter us!

433
00:26:40,349 --> 00:26:42,101
No, but it was looking right at me!

434
00:26:42,184 --> 00:26:46,022
So? It's just a sort
of metal eye thing, it's looking all around.

435
00:26:46,564 --> 00:26:47,648
I don't know. It's like,

436
00:26:47,732 --> 00:26:50,443
it's like there's
something inside, looking at me.

437
00:26:50,526 --> 00:26:53,237
Like, like it knows me.

438
00:26:59,368 --> 00:27:00,536
On my mark.

439
00:27:06,751 --> 00:27:07,835
Open fire!

440
00:27:15,384 --> 00:27:16,761
We've got vision!

441
00:27:21,849 --> 00:27:22,975
It wants us to see.

442
00:28:27,873 --> 00:28:29,125
Fall back! Fall back!

443
00:28:59,321 --> 00:29:01,031
Perhaps it's time for a new strategy.

444
00:29:01,115 --> 00:29:03,367
Maybe we should consider
abandoning this place.

445
00:29:03,451 --> 00:29:06,328
Except there's no power to the helipad, sir.

446
00:29:06,412 --> 00:29:07,955
We can't get out.

447
00:29:08,038 --> 00:29:09,582
You said we could seal the vault?

448
00:29:09,999 --> 00:29:13,753
It was designed to be a bunker
in the event of nuclear war.

449
00:29:13,836 --> 00:29:15,129
- Steel bulkheads...
- There's not enough power!

450
00:29:15,212 --> 00:29:17,465
- Those bulkheads are massive.
- We've got emergency power,

451
00:29:17,548 --> 00:29:18,758
we can reroute that to the bulkhead door.

452
00:29:18,841 --> 00:29:20,176
We'd have to bypass the security codes.

453
00:29:20,301 --> 00:29:21,761
That would take a computer genius.

454
00:29:21,844 --> 00:29:22,887
Good thing you've got me, then.

455
00:29:22,970 --> 00:29:26,140
- You wanna help?
- I don't want to die, Doctor, simple as that.

456
00:29:26,223 --> 00:29:29,143
And nobody knows this software
better than me.

457
00:29:29,226 --> 00:29:30,352
Sir?

458
00:29:31,312 --> 00:29:36,525
<i>I shall speak only to the Doctor.</i>

459
00:29:41,197 --> 00:29:42,865
You're gonna get rusty.

460
00:29:42,990 --> 00:29:49,079
<i>I fed off the DNA of Rose Tyler.</i>

461
00:29:49,205 --> 00:29:55,085
<i>Extrapolating the biomass of a time traveler</i>

462
00:29:55,169 --> 00:29:57,630
<i>regenerated me.</i>

463
00:29:57,713 --> 00:29:58,881
What's your next trick?

464
00:29:59,340 --> 00:30:03,886
<i>I have been searching for the Daleks.</i>

465
00:30:04,094 --> 00:30:05,471
Yeah, I saw.

466
00:30:06,055 --> 00:30:08,557
Downloading the Internet.
What did you find?

467
00:30:08,641 --> 00:30:13,854
I scanned your satellites
and radio telescopes.

468
00:30:14,230 --> 00:30:15,231
And?

469
00:30:15,731 --> 00:30:17,066
<i>Nothing.</i>

470
00:30:18,108 --> 00:30:20,986
<i>Where shall I get my orders now?</i>

471
00:30:21,237 --> 00:30:23,239
You're just a soldier without commands.

472
00:30:23,572 --> 00:30:27,701
<i>Then I shall follow the Primary Order.</i>

473
00:30:27,785 --> 00:30:32,373
<i>The Dalek instinct to destroy. To conquer!</i>

474
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:34,041
What for? What's the point?

475
00:30:37,586 --> 00:30:39,380
Don't you see? It's all gone.

476
00:30:39,463 --> 00:30:42,258
Everything you were,
everything you stood for.

477
00:30:44,093 --> 00:30:46,971
Then what should I do?

478
00:30:49,390 --> 00:30:50,891
All right, then.

479
00:30:51,642 --> 00:30:54,186
If you want orders, follow this one.

480
00:30:57,731 --> 00:30:58,816
Kill yourself.

481
00:30:58,941 --> 00:31:01,026
The Daleks must survive!

482
00:31:01,110 --> 00:31:02,528
The Daleks have failed!

483
00:31:02,611 --> 00:31:05,447
Why don't you finish the job
and make the Daleks extinct?

484
00:31:05,614 --> 00:31:07,241
Rid the universe of your filth!

485
00:31:07,408 --> 00:31:08,868
Why don't you just die?

486
00:31:11,829 --> 00:31:15,916
You would make a good Dalek.

487
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:24,466
Seal the vaults.

488
00:31:33,809 --> 00:31:37,146
I can leech power off the ground
defenses, feed it to the bulkheads.

489
00:31:37,521 --> 00:31:39,231
It's been years since I had to work this fast!

490
00:31:39,315 --> 00:31:40,941
- Are you enjoying this?
- Doctor.

491
00:31:41,025 --> 00:31:42,026
She's still down there.

492
00:31:46,488 --> 00:31:47,698
This isn't the best time!

493
00:31:47,948 --> 00:31:50,117
- Where are you?
- Level 49.

494
00:31:50,743 --> 00:31:54,330
You've got to keep moving.
The vault is being sealed off up at level 46.

495
00:31:54,455 --> 00:31:55,915
Can't you stop them closing?

496
00:31:55,998 --> 00:31:57,124
I'm the one who's closing them.

497
00:31:57,207 --> 00:31:58,834
I can't wait, and I can't help you.

498
00:31:58,918 --> 00:32:00,878
<i>Now for God's sake, run!</i>

499
00:32:09,011 --> 00:32:10,763
Done it! We've got power to the bulkheads.

500
00:32:10,846 --> 00:32:12,473
The Dalek's
right behind them.

501
00:32:13,057 --> 00:32:14,725
We're nearly there! Give us two seconds!

502
00:32:15,100 --> 00:32:16,435
Doctor, I can't sustain the power.

503
00:32:16,518 --> 00:32:18,103
The whole system is failing.

504
00:32:18,187 --> 00:32:19,855
Doctor, you've got to close the bulkheads.

505
00:32:29,782 --> 00:32:30,866
I'm sorry.

506
00:32:37,790 --> 00:32:38,958
Come on!

507
00:33:00,229 --> 00:33:01,397
The vault is sealed.

508
00:33:02,189 --> 00:33:04,775
Rose! Where are you? Rose, did you make it?

509
00:33:10,197 --> 00:33:11,782
Sorry. I was a bit slow.

510
00:33:23,502 --> 00:33:25,421
See you, then, Doctor.

511
00:33:30,092 --> 00:33:31,677
It wasn't your fault.

512
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:33,846
Remember that, okay? It wasn't your fault.

513
00:33:35,806 --> 00:33:37,057
<i>And d'you know what?</i>

514
00:33:38,517 --> 00:33:41,311
I wouldn't have missed it for the world.

515
00:33:52,031 --> 00:33:53,240
<i>DALEK". Exterminate!</i>

516
00:33:58,245 --> 00:33:59,413
I killed her.

517
00:33:59,496 --> 00:34:00,581
I'm sorry.

518
00:34:02,124 --> 00:34:04,043
I said I'd protect her.

519
00:34:04,418 --> 00:34:06,670
She was only here
because of me, and you're sorry?

520
00:34:06,754 --> 00:34:10,632
I could have killed
that Dalek in its cell, but you stopped me.

521
00:34:10,716 --> 00:34:12,426
It was the prize of my collection!

522
00:34:12,509 --> 00:34:15,179
Your collection? Well, was it worth it?

523
00:34:15,596 --> 00:34:18,140
Worth all those men's deaths? Worth Rose?

524
00:34:18,849 --> 00:34:20,434
Let me tell you something, Van Statten.

525
00:34:20,517 --> 00:34:22,811
Mankind goes into space to explore.

526
00:34:22,936 --> 00:34:24,313
To be part of something greater...

527
00:34:24,396 --> 00:34:27,441
Exactly! I wanted to touch the stars.

528
00:34:27,524 --> 00:34:30,152
You just want to drag the stars
down and stick them underground,

529
00:34:30,235 --> 00:34:32,529
underneath tons of sand and dirt,

530
00:34:32,654 --> 00:34:34,323
and label them.

531
00:34:34,656 --> 00:34:37,076
You're about
as far from the stars as you can get.

532
00:34:42,790 --> 00:34:44,792
And you took her down with you.

533
00:34:46,043 --> 00:34:48,003
She was 19 years old.

534
00:34:58,222 --> 00:35:00,057
Go on then, kill me.

535
00:35:03,060 --> 00:35:04,603
Why are you doing this?

536
00:35:04,686 --> 00:35:08,023
I am armed. I will kill.

537
00:35:08,107 --> 00:35:11,151
It is my purpose.

538
00:35:11,235 --> 00:35:12,820
They're all dead because of you!

539
00:35:12,903 --> 00:35:16,406
They are dead because of us!

540
00:35:20,077 --> 00:35:21,537
And now what?

541
00:35:21,662 --> 00:35:23,163
What are you waiting for?

542
00:35:23,247 --> 00:35:28,001
I feel your fear.

543
00:35:28,877 --> 00:35:30,129
What d'you expect?

544
00:35:30,212 --> 00:35:34,049
Daleks do not fear. Must not fear!

545
00:35:37,427 --> 00:35:40,305
You gave me life.

546
00:35:40,931 --> 00:35:45,227
What else have you given me?

547
00:35:45,310 --> 00:35:48,522
I am contaminated.

548
00:35:50,899 --> 00:35:52,985
You were quick on your feet,
leaving Rose behind.

549
00:35:53,068 --> 00:35:55,070
I'm not the one who sealed the vault!

550
00:35:55,195 --> 00:36:00,284
<i>Open the bulkhead or Rose Tyler dies.</i>

551
00:36:02,870 --> 00:36:04,163
You're alive!

552
00:36:04,246 --> 00:36:05,998
<i>Can't get rid of me.</i>

553
00:36:06,081 --> 00:36:07,708
I thought you were dead.

554
00:36:07,791 --> 00:36:10,002
<i>Open the bulkhead!</i>

555
00:36:10,419 --> 00:36:11,503
<i>Don't do it!</i>

556
00:36:11,587 --> 00:36:14,548
<i>What use are emotions,</i>

557
00:36:14,631 --> 00:36:19,803
<i>if you will not save the woman you love?</i>

558
00:36:25,517 --> 00:36:27,269
I killed her once.

559
00:36:28,312 --> 00:36:29,605
I can't do it again.

560
00:36:47,539 --> 00:36:48,582
What do we do now?

561
00:36:48,665 --> 00:36:51,627
You bleeding heart, what the hell do we do?

562
00:36:51,710 --> 00:36:54,046
- Kill it when it gets here.
- All the guns are useless,

563
00:36:54,129 --> 00:36:55,422
and the alien weapons are in the vault.

564
00:36:55,505 --> 00:36:57,507
Only the cataloged ones.

565
00:37:01,929 --> 00:37:03,305
Broken.

566
00:37:04,765 --> 00:37:06,308
Broken.

567
00:37:06,600 --> 00:37:08,101
Hairdryer.

568
00:37:09,019 --> 00:37:11,271
Mr. Van Statten tends to dispose of his staff

569
00:37:11,355 --> 00:37:12,773
and when he does, he wipes their memory.

570
00:37:13,106 --> 00:37:15,651
I kept this stuff in case
I needed to fight my way out one day.

571
00:37:15,734 --> 00:37:16,735
What, you in a fight?

572
00:37:16,818 --> 00:37:18,070
- I'd like to see that.
- I could do!

573
00:37:18,153 --> 00:37:19,738
What you gonna do,
throw your A Levels at 'em?

574
00:37:19,821 --> 00:37:20,989
Oh, yes!

575
00:37:23,158 --> 00:37:24,826
Lock and load!

576
00:37:34,586 --> 00:37:36,463
I'm begging you, don't kill them.
You didn't kill me.

577
00:37:36,546 --> 00:37:37,839
But why not?

578
00:37:39,007 --> 00:37:41,260
Why are you alive?

579
00:37:41,843 --> 00:37:43,971
My function is to kill.

580
00:37:44,054 --> 00:37:47,766
What am I?

581
00:37:54,564 --> 00:37:56,817
Don't move! Don't do anything!

582
00:37:56,942 --> 00:37:58,568
It's beginning to question itself.

583
00:37:59,569 --> 00:38:01,029
Van Statten.

584
00:38:01,530 --> 00:38:03,573
You tortured me.

585
00:38:04,491 --> 00:38:05,867
Why?

586
00:38:05,951 --> 00:38:09,621
I wanted to help you, I just... I don't know,
I was trying to help.

587
00:38:09,705 --> 00:38:12,541
I thought if we could
get through to you, if we could mend you...

588
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:14,293
I wanted you better. I'm sorry.

589
00:38:14,376 --> 00:38:17,879
I'm so sorry. I swear, I just wanted you to talk!

590
00:38:18,297 --> 00:38:20,799
Then hear me talk now.

591
00:38:20,882 --> 00:38:25,470
Exterminate!

592
00:38:25,554 --> 00:38:27,347
Don't do it! Don't kill him!

593
00:38:29,224 --> 00:38:31,059
You don't have to do this anymore.

594
00:38:31,143 --> 00:38:35,063
There must be something else,
not just killing. What else is there?

595
00:38:35,772 --> 00:38:36,982
What do you want?

596
00:38:43,405 --> 00:38:45,407
I want

597
00:38:45,490 --> 00:38:46,908
freedom.

598
00:39:28,075 --> 00:39:30,660
You're out. You made it.

599
00:39:34,247 --> 00:39:36,375
I never thought
I'd feel the sunlight again.

600
00:39:36,458 --> 00:39:41,213
How does it feel?

601
00:40:17,249 --> 00:40:18,750
Get out of the way!

602
00:40:23,004 --> 00:40:24,464
Rose, get out of the way, now!

603
00:40:24,548 --> 00:40:27,342
No! 'Cause I won't let you do this.

604
00:40:27,426 --> 00:40:29,428
That thing killed hundreds of people.

605
00:40:30,554 --> 00:40:32,180
It's not the one pointing the gun at me.

606
00:40:32,556 --> 00:40:35,016
I've got to do this. I've got to end it.

607
00:40:35,100 --> 00:40:37,853
The Daleks destroyed my home, my people.

608
00:40:37,936 --> 00:40:39,729
I've got nothing left.

609
00:40:39,813 --> 00:40:41,022
Look at it.

610
00:40:44,317 --> 00:40:45,360
What's it doing?

611
00:40:48,155 --> 00:40:50,115
It's the sunlight. That's all it wants.

612
00:40:50,198 --> 00:40:51,283
But it can't...

613
00:40:51,366 --> 00:40:54,578
it couldn't kill Van Statten, it couldn't kill me.
It's changing.

614
00:40:56,288 --> 00:40:58,498
And what about you, Doctor?

615
00:40:58,999 --> 00:41:01,168
What the hell are you changing into?

616
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:07,674
I couldn't...

617
00:41:12,095 --> 00:41:13,555
I wasn't...

618
00:41:19,769 --> 00:41:21,188
Oh, Rose.

619
00:41:21,897 --> 00:41:23,482
They're all dead.

620
00:41:23,565 --> 00:41:28,195
Why do we survive?

621
00:41:30,530 --> 00:41:31,656
I don't know.

622
00:41:31,740 --> 00:41:38,747
I am the last of the Daleks.

623
00:41:39,915 --> 00:41:41,541
You're not even that.

624
00:41:43,710 --> 00:41:45,754
Rose did more than regenerate you.

625
00:41:46,421 --> 00:41:48,256
You've absorbed her DNA.

626
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:50,342
You're mutating.

627
00:41:50,967 --> 00:41:53,929
Into what?

628
00:41:55,096 --> 00:41:56,431
Something new.

629
00:41:59,935 --> 00:42:01,228
I'm sorry.

630
00:42:01,311 --> 00:42:03,063
Isn't that better?

631
00:42:03,939 --> 00:42:05,315
Not for a Dalek.

632
00:42:06,525 --> 00:42:10,820
I can feel

633
00:42:10,904 --> 00:42:15,325
so many ideas.

634
00:42:15,408 --> 00:42:19,788
So much darkness.

635
00:42:19,871 --> 00:42:23,583
Rose. Give me orders.

636
00:42:25,544 --> 00:42:28,964
Order me to die.

637
00:42:33,802 --> 00:42:35,136
I can't do that.

638
00:42:35,262 --> 00:42:37,222
This is not life.

639
00:42:39,224 --> 00:42:41,643
This is sickness.

640
00:42:42,561 --> 00:42:46,022
I shall not be like you!

641
00:42:46,898 --> 00:42:48,984
Order my destruction!

642
00:42:51,444 --> 00:42:52,821
Obey!

643
00:42:52,946 --> 00:42:55,574
Obey!

644
00:42:59,035 --> 00:43:00,203
Do it.

645
00:43:02,664 --> 00:43:08,920
Are you frightened, Rose Tyler?

646
00:43:11,798 --> 00:43:13,008
Yeah.

647
00:43:14,801 --> 00:43:17,721
So am I.

648
00:43:19,347 --> 00:43:22,726
Exterminate.

649
00:43:58,762 --> 00:43:59,888
What the hell are you doing?

650
00:44:00,013 --> 00:44:03,725
Two hundred personnel dead,
and all because of you, sir.

651
00:44:03,808 --> 00:44:07,395
Take him away, wipe his memory
and leave him by the road someplace.

652
00:44:07,479 --> 00:44:08,897
You can't do this to me!

653
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:10,398
I am Henry van Statten!

654
00:44:10,565 --> 00:44:13,777
By tonight, Henry van Statten
will be a homeless, brainless junkie,

655
00:44:13,902 --> 00:44:17,822
living on the streets
of San Diego, Seattle, Sacramento.

656
00:44:18,657 --> 00:44:20,617
Some place beginning with "S."

657
00:44:25,246 --> 00:44:27,374
Little piece of home. Better than nothing.

658
00:44:27,957 --> 00:44:30,627
Is that the end of it?
The Time War.

659
00:44:30,752 --> 00:44:31,920
I'm the only one left.

660
00:44:32,629 --> 00:44:35,048
I win. How about that?

661
00:44:36,007 --> 00:44:37,300
The Dalek survived.

662
00:44:37,384 --> 00:44:39,260
Maybe some of your people did, too.

663
00:44:39,344 --> 00:44:40,679
I'd know.

664
00:44:40,762 --> 00:44:41,888
In here.

665
00:44:43,014 --> 00:44:44,766
Feels like there's no one.

666
00:44:45,308 --> 00:44:47,936
Well, then. Good thing
I'm not going anywhere.

667
00:44:48,436 --> 00:44:49,479
Yeah.

668
00:44:49,604 --> 00:44:50,939
We'd better get out.

669
00:44:51,272 --> 00:44:53,817
Van Statten's disappeared.
They're closing down the base.

670
00:44:54,025 --> 00:44:55,860
Goddard says
they're gonna fill it full of cement,

671
00:44:55,944 --> 00:44:57,070
like it never existed!

672
00:44:57,153 --> 00:44:58,238
It's about time.

673
00:44:58,947 --> 00:45:00,115
I'll have to go back home.

674
00:45:00,198 --> 00:45:01,241
Better hurry up, then.

675
00:45:01,324 --> 00:45:03,535
Next flight to Heathrow leaves at 1500 hours.

676
00:45:03,618 --> 00:45:06,746
Adam was saying
that all his life, he wanted to see the stars.

677
00:45:07,288 --> 00:45:08,957
Tell him to go and stand outside, then.

678
00:45:09,624 --> 00:45:12,043
He's all on his own, Doctor. And he did help.

679
00:45:12,127 --> 00:45:13,461
He left you down there!

680
00:45:13,545 --> 00:45:14,587
So did you.

681
00:45:14,671 --> 00:45:16,464
What are you talking about?
We've got to leave!

682
00:45:16,798 --> 00:45:18,216
Plus, he's a bit pretty.

683
00:45:18,299 --> 00:45:19,592
I hadn't noticed.

684
00:45:21,428 --> 00:45:22,512
On your own head.

685
00:45:22,595 --> 00:45:25,682
What are you doing? She said cement.

686
00:45:25,974 --> 00:45:28,727
She wasn't joking, we're gonna get sealed in!

687
00:45:30,562 --> 00:45:31,771
Doctor?

688
00:45:32,313 --> 00:45:35,150
What are you doing standing inside a box?

689
00:45:37,777 --> 00:45:38,945
Rose?

690
00:45:53,168 --> 00:45:55,545
The fourth great and bountiful human empire.

691
00:45:55,837 --> 00:45:57,338
Planet Earth at its height.

692
00:45:59,591 --> 00:46:02,302
Kronkburger with cheese,
kronkburger with pajatos.

693
00:46:02,385 --> 00:46:03,720
Something's wrong.

694
00:46:04,304 --> 00:46:06,014
My watch must be wrong.

695
00:46:06,097 --> 00:46:07,265
That's what comes with showing off.

696
00:46:07,348 --> 00:46:08,725
Your history's not as good
as you thought it was.

697
00:46:08,850 --> 00:46:09,934
My history's perfect.

698
00:46:10,018 --> 00:46:11,269
Well, obviously not.

699
00:46:11,352 --> 00:46:12,812
I can taste it.

700
00:46:12,896 --> 00:46:14,272
Engage safety.

701
00:46:14,355 --> 00:46:16,316
<i>Someone down there
shouldn't be here.</i>

702
00:46:19,986 --> 00:46:21,279
<i>Who are you?</i>

703
00:46:21,362 --> 00:46:23,072
I'm the editor.

704
00:46:23,156 --> 00:46:24,199
What's happening?

705
00:46:24,407 --> 00:46:25,700
And spike.
